---
import DocumentLayout from '../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro';
import LeadStrand from '../components/LeadStrand.astro';
import Receipt from '../components/Receipt.astro';
import Needs from '../components/Needs.astro';
import Draft from '../components/Draft.astro';
import SurfaceLedger from '../components/SurfaceLedger.astro';

/**
 * Every figure here is countable from the source directories, and every quoted
 * feedback line is verbatim from FEEDBACK.md. The v5→v6 diff was read directly;
 * nothing about what "landed" is inferred from the checkboxes, which were all
 * left unticked.
 */
const counts = [
  { n: '48', label: 'itemised notes' },
  { n: '6', label: 'surfaces reviewed' },
  { n: '394', label: 'lines changed next' },
  { n: '4', label: 'files touched' },
];

// Verbatim from FEEDBACK.md, one per reviewed surface.
const notes = [
  'Add curved border/radius around table',
  'Rename “Executive Intervention Queue” to “Intervention Queue”',
  'Progress visuals: Fix color coding — exceeding target vs falling behind should use different colors',
  'Add summary metrics above table: Total Jobs, Open, Paused, Done, Policy Adherence',
  'Animate AI “thinking” before showing results (gathering info from different apps)',
  'Add sticky columns (first 3) for horizontal scroll',
];
---

<DocumentLayout
  title="What a review looks like when the thing being reviewed runs"
  metaTitle="The review loop — feedback against working software | Tyler Young"
  description="Forty-eight itemised notes taken against a running build, and the diff that shows exactly which ones were acted on and which were not."
  descriptionDraft
  eyebrow="Review Loop"
  meta={[
    ['Artifact', 'One feedback round · 48 items · 6 surfaces'],
    ['Response', '4 files · 394 lines, in the next version'],
    ['Method', 'Review against a deployed build, not a mockup'],
    ['Client', '[NEEDS: naming decision — not shown here either way]'],
  ]}
>
  <p class="answer">
    <Draft>
      A stakeholder sat with a running build and produced forty-eight specific
      notes, organised by surface. The next version changed four files and three
      hundred and ninety-four lines. Both artifacts still exist, so the whole
      exchange is auditable — including the parts that were not acted on.
    </Draft>
  </p>

  <dl class="counts">
    {
      counts.map((c) => (
        <div>
          <dt>{c.n}</dt>
          <dd>{c.label}</dd>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </dl>

  <h2>The notes are specific because the thing was real</h2>
  <p>
    <Draft>
      Nobody writes “add sticky columns to the first three” about a picture of a
      table. You write it after trying to scroll one. The register of this feedback
      is the argument for the method — it is the language of someone using
      software, not evaluating a proposal.
    </Draft>
  </p>

  <ul class="notes">
    {notes.map((n) => <li>{n}</li>)}
  </ul>
  <p class="src">Six of forty-eight, verbatim</p>

  <Receipt
    label="FEEDBACK.md → the next version"
    leftLabel="What the reviewer asked for"
    rightLabel="What changed in the code"
    caption="Read from the v5→v6 diff directly. The checkboxes in the feedback file were never ticked — the code is the record."
  >
    <div slot="left">
      <pre><span class="dim">## Jobs</span>

- [ ] Add curved border/radius
      around table

<span class="dim">## Home</span>

- [ ] Rename "Executive Intervention
      Queue" to "Intervention Queue"

- [ ] Fix color coding — exceeding
      target vs falling behind should
      use different colors</pre>
    </div>
    <div slot="right">
      <pre><span class="cue">+</span> borderBottomLeftRadius: 8
<span class="cue">+</span> borderBottomRightRadius: 8
  <span class="dim">…8 radius declarations added,
   none removed</span>

<span class="cue">+</span> label: 'Intervention Queue'
<span class="cue">-</span> label: 'Executive Intervention…'

<span class="cue">+</span> 'Amber threshold'
  <span class="dim">…6 colour-threshold changes</span></pre>
    </div>
  </Receipt>

  <div class="ledger-slot"><SurfaceLedger /></div>

  <h2>The interesting part is what did not change</h2>
  <p>
    <Draft>
      Five component files were left untouched — the AI response panel, the drawer,
      the live session view, and both navigation components. The notes covering
      those surfaces are still sitting in the file, unactioned.
    </Draft>
  </p>
  <p>
    <Draft>
      That is not a failure of the round. A review produces a queue, not a checklist
      to be emptied, and someone decided which half of it was worth a version. What
      is unusual is that the decision is legible at all. Review a mockup and there
      is no diff to read; the prioritisation lives in someone's memory. Review
      running code and it becomes a record.
    </Draft>
  </p>

  <div class="aside">
    <p>
      No screens from this build are shown. It carries a named end customer and
      their dealer network throughout, and has not been sanitised. The feedback
      lines and the diff excerpts above contain none of it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>What happened after</h2>
  <p>
    <Needs>
      Tyler — whether the remaining items were picked up in a later round, and how
      many rounds this surface went through in total. The directories suggest six
      versions; that is not the same as six review rounds.
    </Needs>
  </p>

  <LeadStrand
    slot="after"
    items={[
      {
        slug: 'how-i-shaped-cross-functional-reputation',
        note: 'Reviewing on working code changes what the rest of the org thinks design is for. It is a reputational move before it is a technical one, and it only works if design is already trusted in planning.',
      },
      {
        slug: 'how-i-built-culture-around-paradox',
        note: 'Forty-eight notes and four changed files is a judgement about which half mattered. Knowing which quality bars are load-bearing is the whole discipline of shipping inside a fixed window.',
      },
    ]}
  />
</DocumentLayout>

<style>
  .answer {
    font-size: 24px !important;
    line-height: 1.52 !important;
    margin-bottom: 36px !important;
  }

  .counts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 22px 20px;
    margin: 0 0 40px;
    padding: 24px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .counts div {
    display: grid;
    gap: 4px;
  }

  .counts dt {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(30px, 5vw, 40px);
    font-weight: 620;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .counts dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-ink-3);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .notes {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0 0 10px !important;
    padding: 0 !important;
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .notes li {
    font-family: var(--font-mono) !important;
    font-size: 13px !important;
    line-height: 1.6 !important;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    color: var(--color-ink-2);
    padding: 10px 14px !important;
    background: var(--color-paper-sunk);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-rule-strong);
  }

  .notes li::before {
    content: none !important;
  }

  .ledger-slot {
    margin: 0 0 34px;
  }

  .src {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px !important;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-ink-3);
    margin: 0 0 34px !important;
  }

  @media (min-width: 810px) {
    .counts {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
</style>
